    /// permission to modify the object.
    /// You may supply `fields` (a full or partial key-value map to merge into the
    /// object), `field_ops` (granular array operations per field), `acl`, or any
    /// compatible combination. The same field name must not appear in both
    /// `fields` and `field_ops`, which returns 422. Returns 404 if the object does
    /// not exist or has been deleted.
    /// Use `expected_version` for optimistic concurrency: if the object's current
    /// `aggregate_version` does not match, the request returns 409 and does not
    /// retry the caller write. Omit it to keep the existing OCC merge retry.
    ///
    /// - Parameters:
    ///   - object: Custom object ID (`cobj_...`) to update.
    ///   - input: Request body.
    /// - Returns: Successful response
    public func replace(object: String, input: CustomObjectReplaceInput) async throws -> CustomObjectReplaceResponse {
        return try await http.request("/api/v1/custom_objects/\(object)", method: "PUT", body: input)
    }
}
